      "difficulty": "Hard",
      "prompt": "$\\lim_{x\\to 1}\\dfrac{x^3-1}{x^2-1}=?$\nA) $\\dfrac{2}{3}$\nB) $\\dfrac{3}{2}$\nC) $1$\nD) $3$",
      "answer": "B) $\\dfrac{3}{2}$",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Factor: $\\frac{(x-1)(x^2+x+1)}{(x-1)(x+1)}=\\frac{x^2+x+1}{x+1}$.",
          "Substitute $x=1$: $\\frac{3}{2}$. Key is B.",
          "A) inverts the fraction.",
          "C) and D) are miscounts of the factors."
        ],
        "answer": "B) $\\dfrac{3}{2}$"
      }
