      "prompt": "$\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\dfrac{\\sqrt{4+x}-\\sqrt{4-x}}{x}=?$\nA) $0$\nB) $\\dfrac{1}{2}$\nC) $1$\nD) $2$",
      "answer": "B) $\\dfrac{1}{2}$",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Rationalize: multiply by $\\frac{\\sqrt{4+x}+\\sqrt{4-x}}{\\sqrt{4+x}+\\sqrt{4-x}}$; numerator becomes $(4+x)-(4-x)=2x$.",
          "Get $\\frac{2x}{x(\\sqrt{4+x}+\\sqrt{4-x})}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4+x}+\\sqrt{4-x}}$.",
          "Substitute $x=0$: $\\frac{2}{2+2}=\\frac{1}{2}$. Key is B.",
          "A), C), D) miss the conjugate step."
